# Trainer card revisions

Every insert or update of `trainer_profiles` keeps a post-image of the card text and the card fields. The row is the state after the write. A card keeps the newest 12. Older rows are deleted in that same write.

This is not the operational journal. `app_logs` still gets one short `trainer.revision` row. The snapshot and the diff live in `trainer_revisions`.

## What is stored

The snapshot is the visible card: name, headline, bio, source text, about, pinned captions, sports, city, addresses, price, experience, contacts, hide flags, photos, and certificates. Status and verification are included.

Do not store `claim_token`, `preview_token`, `edit_token`, or `claim_path`. Do not put the bio, a phone, or a token in the `app_logs` row. That row names the source and the field keys.

## How a write is marked

The capture is a PostgreSQL `AFTER INSERT OR UPDATE` trigger. It still stores the snapshot when the application forgets to mark the actor. The source is then `write` and the actor is empty.

When the writer knows who did it, set the mark inside the same transaction as the update. `set_config(..., true)` is transaction-local. A session-level setting leaks across the pool.

```ts
await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
  await stampTrainerRevision(tx, "cabinet", userId);
  await tx.update(trainerProfiles).set(values).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, id));
});
```

Sources: `admin`, `cabinet`, `sync`, `import`, `door`, `write`.

## Who can read it

Staff only. `listTrainerRevisionViews` runs behind `assertStaff` on the trainer page. The «История» tab on `/admin/trainers/$slug` shows the diff. A trainer cabinet does not.

Install with `npm run trainers:revisions`. Do not use `db:push` for this table. The first install stores the current card once, as `baseline`, so the next edit has a previous copy. Re-running the script does not add a second baseline.

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: the setting outlives the query on a pooled connection
await db.execute(sql`select set_config('trenio.revision_actor', ${userId}, false)`);
await db.update(trainerProfiles).set(values);

// wrong: the diff is assembled in the browser from the live card
<TrainerHistory trainer={trainer} />
```
